                <pb facs="0359" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383 J 41/75: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-04T16:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:03 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>468. The following telegram has been received from Consular Agent Jenkins at
                    Puebla dated today: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Federal Judge rendered decision in my case this morning declaring that
                            all proof against me had disappeared and placing me in liberty canceling
                            my bond. I have certified copy of his decision which I will deliver to
                            you Monday.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
